\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{1}{8}{Schematic of the self-starting siphon geometry. The container water level $h_c^{(0)}$ lies between the first crest $B$ and main crest $D$. Node $A$ is the inlet; segment $A \to B$ fills hydrostatically. The drop $B \to C$ builds momentum. The climb $C \to D$ passes above the waterline. Point $W$ on segment $D \to E$ marks the last waterline crossing}{figure.1}{}}
